Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Fault-Tolerant Gadgets, from the Cat State to FT(C)", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell["\<\
A quantum error-correcting code tells you which errors you could detect. It \
does not tell you how to detect them without causing more, and that gap is \
the whole subject of fault tolerance: the circuit that measures a check is \
built from the same failing gates as everything else, and one bad gate inside \
it can spread into many bad qubits on the data.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell["\<\
This note is about the six gadgets that close that gap, in the order they \
build on each other. Each one is an object you can hold, ask questions of, \
and hand to the next:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"], Cell["", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],
     Cell["gadget", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],
     Cell["what it is", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
