  }]], "3ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The thread running through them is that every claim is ",
 StyleBox["measured rather than cited",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". \"This gadget is fault tolerant\" becomes a number: how many data errors \
one fault leaves behind. \"This is the logical CNOT\" becomes a conjugation \
you can read off. \"This protocol costs more\" becomes the three overheads of \
Definition 10.6. And where a gadget does ",
 StyleBox["not", "TI"],
 " deliver what its name suggests, it says so \[LongDash] one of the objects \
below reports ",
 Cell[BoxData["False"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],
 " for exactly the reason the book gives."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],

Cell["Definition", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The code layer is a development package under ",
 Cell["OngoingProjects/QEC/", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],
 ", not yet part of the paclet, so this page loads both the framework and the \
layer itself. Symbols introduced in this section stay bound for the whole \
note."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],

